With **.NET 10 SDK**, you get native MTP support in `dotnet test` — **no, you do not need `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport`**. That property is only for .NET 9 and earlier.

Instead, add a `test` section to your `global.json`:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

With this in place, `dotnet test` passes arguments directly to MTP (e.g., `dotnet test --report-trx`) — no `--` separator needed.

**Key differences from .NET 9 setup:**

| .NET 9 (old) | .NET 10 (new) |
|---|---|
| `<TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>true</TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>` in Directory.Build.props | `"test": { "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform" }` in global.json |
| `dotnet test -- --report-trx` (separator required) | `dotnet test --report-trx` (direct) |

You still need the framework-specific runner enablement (`EnableMSTestRunner`, `EnableNUnitRunner`, etc.) and `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>` — those are unchanged. Want me to update your project files?
